# handwritten_copy.manifest — THE authoritative list of hand-written
# lean_frontend/*.lean files that `make lean-prelude-src` copies into
# lean_frontend/generated/ (Lake compiles from generated/ — lakefile.toml
# srcDir — NOT from lean_frontend/). One basename per line; lines
# starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Read by (single point of truth; nothing else enumerates this set):
#   Makefile               LEAN_HANDWRITTEN (the copy recipe itself)
#   tools/check_handwritten_sync.sh   the byte-identity gate, wired into
#                          tools/check_driver_fresh.sh (--record-lean /
#                          --check[-lean]), scripts/common.sh build_lean
#                          (precondition) and scripts/test_unit.sh.
# The gate ALSO fails if a lean_frontend/*.lean exists that is not listed
# here (an unlisted hand-written file would never be propagated), so the
# manifest cannot silently drift from the tree. An empty manifest is a
# FAIL, not a vacuous pass.
#
# Origin: hotfix fix/freshness-copy-gap (2026-09-02) — the driver-
# freshness stamp hashed both the hand-written file and its generated/
# copy but never compared them, so a build_lean without lean-prelude-src
# recorded a green stamp over a binary built from a stale copy
# (lean_frontend/docs/2026-09-02_freshness-copy-gap.md).
